{"id": "EUVD-2026-103774", "enisaUuid": "14bef1ae-4c9d-3f07-a40a-836eb354821e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmtd: core: avoid double-free of OTP NVMEM device\n\nIf factory OTP setup fails after the user OTP NVMEM device has been\nregistered, mtd_otp_nvmem_add() unregisters the user device but leaves\nmtd->otp_user_nvmem set. On an error, the caller unregisters it again.\nFor -EOPNOTSUPP, registration continues and normal teardown unregisters\nit again.\n\nClear mtd->otp_user_nvmem after unregistering it.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:49:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:26:26", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cecf007418b93a2cbc94269e07fe2fb28f54d8fb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/26300879cd8e4612dce66bb8f6ff7cd35fcf3e59"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98834", "GHSA-cqw6-frjh-g7f6"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "08dc40ad-2b90-33e5-b404-01c0f189b04f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "dd6c85f98ff33b009b819090268cbf679dc208b9"}, {"id": "0bfd44e3-e047-354d-ba00-8fb630d94b07", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.28 <6.2"}, {"id": "17e04da8-dcdf-3c0d-ae88-a1a03d97b5e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "949476b8601bde5459048eebdf457c9db20addd8"}, {"id": "42f8da1a-07a1-310b-b49a-6217d934a4d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "4fe38539-ace5-3cdb-89d9-3ebcd355de72", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.111 <5.16"}, {"id": "5c237905-4c45-3a32-82c3-0ef3f64a51b1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e0489f6e221f5ddee6cb3bd51b992b790c5fa4b9 <26300879cd8e4612dce66bb8f6ff7cd35fcf3e59"}, {"id": "6143690c-897b-3ab6-a7b9-de3930e5b548", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor